  <h2>What this is</h2>
  <p>
    The Mind pillar opens with a question most health programs skip entirely: why does
    any of this matter to you? Men in mid-life often find themselves achieving external
    markers while feeling vaguely disconnected from what those markers were supposed to
    produce. That disconnect is metabolically real — purposelessness correlates with
    elevated inflammatory markers and accelerated cognitive aging.
  </p>
  <p>
    We use a structured goal-setting framework that bridges your 10-year vision to the
    choices you make this week. The My4MLife App walks you through this in Month 1,
    Week 1, and revisits it at the end of each month.
  </p>
  <p>Naming your accountability target is also a MindSpan input — men who anchor their goals to a specific face tend to show stronger momentum in their score than those working from an abstract "get healthier."</p>

  <h2>Our approach</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Vision Mapping</h3>
      <p>Articulate the end in mind — health, relationships, legacy — in specific, sensory language.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>90-Day Goals</h3>
      <p>Translate the vision into three 90-day objectives with leading-indicator metrics.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Weekly Review Ritual</h3>
      <p>A 10-minute Sunday review built into the My4MLife App keeps drift from compounding.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Accountability Community</h3>
      <p>Peer accountability inside the member community amplifies follow-through in ways solo plans can't match.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
